Uncertainty, model discrepancy and an electromagnetic claim (@em-uncertainty: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91", #source "../sources/Experimental-Physics-MIT-Junior-Lab.lingua#r_55H9HGYP31B14NSEEAZY27PW5E", #electromagnetism "../connections/Fields-through-mining-metals-utilities-devices-and-information.lingua#r_205SB4K06PDYXA7YGX3Q8X0YMW") { r_2KYWTMX0SHJYWAH69AQ9H3068X
**Read:** [Measuring Permittivity and Permeability — NIST TN 1536](../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91), uncertainty, specimen and calibration analyses; [Experimental Physics I and II — MIT Junior Lab](../sources/Experimental-Physics-MIT-Junior-Lab.lingua#r_55H9HGYP31B14NSEEAZY27PW5E), complete reporting and uncertainty guidance for the chosen experiment.

State an operational claim such as a resonance frequency, shielding attenuation, transmitted power or material response over a specified band. Define the measurand, environmental conditions, reference planes and decision use. Separate input/calibration uncertainty, numerical approximation, repeatability and discrepancy between the ideal model and the actual object.

Use complex covariance when amplitude and phase or real/imaginary parts are correlated. Report how phase unwrapping, background subtraction, fixture removal and model selection influence the result. A single scalar uncertainty added after fitting cannot automatically represent ambiguous inverse solutions or an omitted mode.

Compare two models and at least one alternative apparatus condition. If they disagree beyond their stated uncertainty, investigate assumptions before averaging. Preserve evidence that changed the conclusion and a sensitivity analysis of the final claim. The reused metrology Record supplies the general method; this application adds field geometry, material response and frequency-dependent evidence. Exact numerical energy conservation verifies an implementation property, while agreement with an independent physical measurement tests a broader and still limited claim about the world.

